<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa 9-mo pre-tax profit falls 14 pct.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa 9-mo pre-tax profit falls 14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     434     vs 506</p>
<p>    Group operating profit		   408     vs 523</p>
<p>    Group financial result		   26 gain vs 17 charge</p>
<p>    Group sales				  15,193  vs 14,250</p>
<p>    Traffic revenue			    13,593  vs 12,948</p>
<p>    --passenger revenue			11,174  vs 10,529</p>
<p>    --freight including mail		 2,419   vs 2,419</p>
<p>    --other revenue			    1,600   vs 1,302</p>
<p>    Cost of materials			  6,649   vs 6,055</p>
<p>    --of which fuel costs		    1,265   vs 1,072</p>
<p>    Personnel expenses			 4,157   vs 3,831</p>
<p>    Depreciation				 996     vs 988</p>
<p>    Other operating expenses		 3,926   vs 3,866</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German national airline is Deutsche Lufthansa AG. Analysts had expected a fall in nine-month profits, with forecasts focusing on a pre-tax profit figure pf 440 to 460 million marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
